/*!
@defgroup acmp
@ingroup mod_analog Analog Comparator (ACMP)
@brief Analog voltage comparison and threshold-detection module for the YTMicro SDK.

@details
The ACMP module compares two analog inputs and reports the result through a
digital output, interrupt request, DMA trigger, or continuous scan status.
It can compare two external channels directly, or compare an external input
against the integrated DAC threshold generated inside the peripheral.

@section acmp_features Key Features
- Single-ended analog comparison with programmable output polarity.
- Selectable edge detection for interrupts and DMA requests.
- Configurable hysteresis, power mode, and optional hard-block offset control.
- Integrated DAC threshold generator with configurable output level.
- Flexible positive and negative input routing through external MUX channels
  or the internal DAC path.
- Optional digital filter with programmable sample period, sample count, and
  selectable filter clock source.
- Continuous scan support for multi-channel round-robin sampling with
  per-channel expectation settings.
- Device-dependent options controlled by `FEATURE_ACMP_*` macros, such as
  dedicated clock selection, DAC output enable, level detection, or
  continuous-mode implementation details.

@section acmp_modes Supported Modes

The ACMP driver exposes the sample and runtime modes listed below:

| Mode / Path | Driver Enum / API | Description |
|-------------|-------------------|-------------|
| Common compare | ACMP_COMMON_MODE | Standard comparator operation on the selected positive and negative inputs. |
| Trigger mode | ACMP_TRIGGER_MODE | Sampled comparison mode driven by the peripheral timing configuration. |
| Window mode | ACMP_WINDOW_MODE | Windowed comparison mode when supported by the device. |
| Continuous scan | ACMP_CONTINUOUS_MODE or ACMP_DRV_EnableContinuous() | Scans multiple channels in round-robin order and records channel-specific results. |
| DAC threshold compare | ACMP_INPUT_SRC_DAC | Routes the integrated DAC output to one comparator input for threshold detection. |
| External pin compare | ACMP_INPUT_SRC_MUX | Routes external analog channels to comparator inputs through the MUX. |

@section acmp_arch Module Architecture

The ACMP module is organized in a two-layer architecture:

@verbatim
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Application Code                │
│        (calls ACMP_DRV_* functions)          │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│       ACMP Driver Layer (acmp_driver.h/c)    │
│  ● Instance-based API (init, config, flags)  │
│  ● Aggregates comparator, DAC, MUX, and      │
│    continuous-mode configuration blocks      │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│    ACMP HW Access Layer (acmp_hw_access.h/c) │
│  ● Register-level helpers for comparator,    │
│    DAC, filter, and continuous mode control  │
│  ● Inline accessors for performance-critical │
│    register reads and writes                 │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│           ACMP Peripheral Hardware           │
│      (CTRL, DAC, MUX, FILT, CONT, STS)       │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection acmp_arch_driver Driver Layer (acmp_driver.h)
Application code should use the `ACMP_DRV_*` APIs. The driver resolves the
hardware base address from the instance index and applies configuration through
four sub-structures bundled in `acmp_config_t`:
- `acmp_comparator_config_t`
- `acmp_dac_config_t`
- `acmp_mux_config_t`
- `acmp_continuous_config_t`

@subsection acmp_arch_hw HW Access Layer (acmp_hw_access.h)
The internal HW access layer provides low-level register helpers grouped into:
- Comparator core control
- Input routing
- Interrupt and DMA control
- DAC control
- Filter control
- Continuous mode control
- Status and lifecycle helpers

@section acmp_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection acmp_config_root acmp_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| comparatorConfig | acmp_comparator_config_t * | Points to the comparator core settings block. Must reference writable storage when used with ACMP_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() or ACMP_DRV_GetConfigAll(). |
| dacConfig | acmp_dac_config_t * | Points to the DAC settings block. |
| muxConfig | acmp_mux_config_t * | Points to the input routing settings block. |
| continuousConfig | acmp_continuous_config_t * | Points to the continuous scan settings block. |

@subsection acmp_config_comparator acmp_comparator_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default Value |
|-------|------|-------------|---------------|
| sampleMode | acmp_sample_mode_t | Comparator operating mode. | ACMP_COMMON_MODE |
| edgeSelection | acmp_edge_select_t | Edge or level condition used for output events. | ACMP_RISING_EDGE |
| hysteresisLevel | acmp_hysteresis_t | Internal hysteresis setting. | ACMP_HYS_LEVEL_0 |
| hardBlockOffset | bool | Enables symmetric hysteresis handling when supported. | false |
| outputSelect | acmp_output_select_t | Chooses filtered or direct output path to the pin. | ACMP_OUTPUT_DIRECTLY |
| outputPolarity | acmp_output_polarity_t | Output inversion control. | ACMP_OUT_POL_NOT_INVERT |
| powerMode | acmp_power_mode_t | Comparator speed or power trade-off. | ACMP_LOW_POWER |
| filterEnable | bool | Enables the digital filter path. | false |
| filterClkSrc | acmp_filter_clk_src_t | Filter clock source when filtering is enabled. | ACMP_FILTER_SEL_FUNC_CLK |
| filterSamplePeriod | uint8_t | Filter sampling period in peripheral clock cycles. | 0 |
| filterSampleCount | uint8_t | Number of agreeing samples required by the filter. | 0 |
| autoDisableHardBlock | bool | Auto-disables the hard block in one-shot mode when supported. | false |
| acmpClkSrc | acmp_clock_source_t | ACMP module clock source when supported. | ACMP_CLK_SRC_SIRC |
| interruptEnable | bool | Enables comparator interrupt signaling. | true |
| dmaTriggerEnable | bool | Enables comparator DMA triggering. | false |

@subsection acmp_config_dac acmp_dac_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default Value |
|-------|------|-------------|---------------|
| voltageReferenceSource | acmp_voltage_reference_t | DAC reference source when supported. | Device-dependent |
| enable | bool | Enables the integrated DAC threshold generator. | true |
| outputEnable | bool | Enables DAC output visibility when supported. | Device-dependent |
| voltage | uint8_t | DAC threshold code written to the peripheral. | 127 |

@subsection acmp_config_mux acmp_mux_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default Value |
|-------|------|-------------|---------------|
| positiveInputSrc | acmp_input_source_t | Source routed to the positive comparator input. | ACMP_INPUT_SRC_MUX |
| negativeInputSrc | acmp_input_source_t | Source routed to the negative comparator input. | ACMP_INPUT_SRC_MUX |
| positiveInputChnSel | acmp_ch_number_t | External channel index for the positive input when MUX is selected. | 0 |
| negativeInputChnSel | acmp_ch_number_t | External channel index for the negative input when MUX is selected. | 1 |

@subsection acmp_config_continuous acmp_continuous_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default Value |
|-------|------|-------------|---------------|
| continuousEnable | bool | Enables continuous scan mode. | false |
| continuousMode | acmp_continuous_mode_t | Loop or one-shot scan behavior. | ACMP_CONTINUOUS_LOOP_MODE |
| oneshotTriggerEnable | bool | Enables one-shot trigger gating when supported. | false |
| fixedPort | acmp_fixed_port_t | Selects which comparator input remains fixed during scan. | ACMP_FIXED_NEG_PORT |
| samplePeriod | uint8_t | Channel-to-channel scan period. | FEATURE_ACMP_DEFAULT_CONT_PERIOD |
| samplePosition | uint8_t | Delay before each sample to allow input settling. | FEATURE_ACMP_DEFAULT_CONT_POS |
| continuousInterruptEnable | bool | Enables interrupt reporting for continuous mode. | false |
| channelConfig[8] | acmp_ch_config_t[8] | Per-channel enable and expected compare state. | Disabled, expectation = ACMP_EXPECT_POS_LESS_THAN_NEG |

@subsection acmp_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| FEATURE_ACMP_HAS_CLK_SRC_SEL | Device supports explicit ACMP clock source selection. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_HAS_AUTODIS | Device supports auto-disable hard block in one-shot mode. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_HAS_OFFSET_CONTROL | Device supports hard-block offset configuration. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_HAS_DAC_OUTPUT | Device supports enabling DAC analog output. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_HAS_DAC_VOLTAGE_REF_SRC | Device supports selecting the DAC reference source. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_HAS_FILTER_BYPASS | Device exposes an explicit filter bypass control bit. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_HAS_FILTER_CLK_SRC_IN_CTRL_REG | Filter clock source is stored in CTRL instead of FILT. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_HAS_CONTINUOUS_MODE_IN_CTRL_REG | Continuous mode is selected through the CTRL mode field. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_HAS_TRIG_MODE_GATE | One-shot continuous mode supports trigger gating. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_SUPPORT_LEVEL_DETECTION | Output flag reporting also supports high-level and low-level events. |
| FEATURE_ACMP_DEFAULT_CONT_PERIOD | Default continuous scan period used by ACMP_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(). |
| FEATURE_ACMP_DEFAULT_CONT_POS | Default continuous sample position used by ACMP_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(). |

@section acmp_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection acmp_usage_basic Pattern 1: Basic External Input Comparison
Use the default configuration as a starting point, route two external channels
through the MUX, then enable the comparator and read the output state.

@code{.c}
#define INST_ACMP (0U)

acmp_comparator_config_t comparatorConfig;
acmp_dac_config_t dacConfig;
acmp_mux_config_t muxConfig;
acmp_continuous_config_t continuousConfig;
acmp_config_t acmpConfig =
{
    .comparatorConfig = &comparatorConfig,
    .dacConfig = &dacConfig,
    .muxConfig = &muxConfig,
    .continuousConfig = &continuousConfig
};

ACMP_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&acmpConfig);

/* Compare external channel 0 against external channel 1. */
muxConfig.positiveInputSrc = ACMP_INPUT_SRC_MUX;
muxConfig.negativeInputSrc = ACMP_INPUT_SRC_MUX;
muxConfig.positiveInputChnSel = 0U;
muxConfig.negativeInputChnSel = 1U;
dacConfig.enable = false;

ACMP_DRV_Init(INST_ACMP, &acmpConfig);
ACMP_DRV_Enable(INST_ACMP);

if (ACMP_DRV_GetOutput(INST_ACMP))
{
    /* Positive input is currently above the negative input. */
}

ACMP_DRV_Disable(INST_ACMP);
@endcode

@subsection acmp_usage_dac Pattern 2: DAC Threshold Comparison
Use the integrated DAC as one comparator input to implement a programmable
analog threshold detector.

@code{.c}
#define INST_ACMP (0U)

acmp_comparator_config_t comparatorConfig;
acmp_dac_config_t dacConfig;
acmp_mux_config_t muxConfig;
acmp_continuous_config_t continuousConfig;
acmp_config_t acmpConfig =
{
    .comparatorConfig = &comparatorConfig,
    .dacConfig = &dacConfig,
    .muxConfig = &muxConfig,
    .continuousConfig = &continuousConfig
};

ACMP_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&acmpConfig);

/* Compare external channel 2 against the DAC threshold. */
muxConfig.positiveInputSrc = ACMP_INPUT_SRC_MUX;
muxConfig.negativeInputSrc = ACMP_INPUT_SRC_DAC;
muxConfig.positiveInputChnSel = 2U;
dacConfig.enable = true;
dacConfig.voltage = 96U;
comparatorConfig.edgeSelection = ACMP_BOTH_EDGES;

ACMP_DRV_Init(INST_ACMP, &acmpConfig);
ACMP_DRV_Enable(INST_ACMP);

/* Read and clear output event flags after an edge-triggered wakeup or ISR. */
uint8_t outputFlags = 0U;
ACMP_DRV_GetOutputFlags(INST_ACMP, &outputFlags);
ACMP_DRV_ClearOutputFlags(INST_ACMP);

ACMP_DRV_Disable(INST_ACMP);
@endcode

@subsection acmp_usage_continuous Pattern 3: Continuous Multi-Channel Scan
Enable continuous mode to scan several external channels in round-robin order
while keeping one comparator input fixed.

@code{.c}
#define INST_ACMP (0U)

acmp_comparator_config_t comparatorConfig;
acmp_dac_config_t dacConfig;
acmp_mux_config_t muxConfig;
acmp_continuous_config_t continuousConfig;
acmp_config_t acmpConfig =
{
    .comparatorConfig = &comparatorConfig,
    .dacConfig = &dacConfig,
    .muxConfig = &muxConfig,
    .continuousConfig = &continuousConfig
};

ACMP_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&acmpConfig);

continuousConfig.continuousEnable = true;
continuousConfig.continuousMode = ACMP_CONTINUOUS_LOOP_MODE;
continuousConfig.fixedPort = ACMP_FIXED_NEG_PORT;
continuousConfig.continuousInterruptEnable = true;
continuousConfig.channelConfig[0].enable = true;
continuousConfig.channelConfig[0].expectation = ACMP_EXPECT_POS_GREAT_THAN_NEG;
continuousConfig.channelConfig[1].enable = true;
continuousConfig.channelConfig[1].expectation = ACMP_EXPECT_POS_LESS_THAN_NEG;

ACMP_DRV_Init(INST_ACMP, &acmpConfig);
ACMP_DRV_Enable(INST_ACMP);

acmp_ch_list_t changedChannels = 0U;
ACMP_DRV_GetChannelFlags(INST_ACMP, &changedChannels);
ACMP_DRV_ClearChannelFlags(INST_ACMP);

/* Read the most recently sampled channel and its output state. */
uint8_t channelId = ACMP_DRV_GetChannelId(INST_ACMP);
bool channelOutput = ACMP_DRV_GetChannelOutput(INST_ACMP, channelId);
(void)channelOutput;

ACMP_DRV_DisableContinuous(INST_ACMP);
ACMP_DRV_Disable(INST_ACMP);
@endcode

@section acmp_api API Quick Reference

@subsection acmp_api_init Initialization & Global Control
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| ACMP_DRV_Reset() | Resets the selected ACMP instance through IPC software reset control. |
| ACMP_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() | Populates all ACMP sub-configuration blocks with driver defaults. |
| ACMP_DRV_Init() | Applies comparator, DAC, MUX, and optional continuous-mode settings. |
| ACMP_DRV_Enable() | Enables the comparator block after configuration. |
| ACMP_DRV_Disable() | Disables the comparator block. |

@subsection acmp_api_config Configuration
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| ACMP_DRV_GetConfigAll() | Reads back all configured ACMP sub-block settings. |
| ACMP_DRV_ConfigComparator() | Applies comparator core settings. |
| ACMP_DRV_GetComparatorConfig() | Reads back comparator core settings. |
| ACMP_DRV_ConfigDac() | Configures the integrated DAC threshold generator. |
| ACMP_DRV_GetDacConfig() | Reads back DAC settings. |
| ACMP_DRV_ConfigMux() | Selects the positive and negative comparator input routes. |
| ACMP_DRV_GetMuxConfig() | Reads back the input routing configuration. |
| ACMP_DRV_ConfigContinuous() | Configures continuous scan behavior and per-channel expectations. |
| ACMP_DRV_GetContinuousConfig() | Reads back continuous scan configuration. |

@subsection acmp_api_runtime Continuous Runtime Control
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| ACMP_DRV_SetExpectation() | Updates the packed channel expectation bitmap for continuous mode. |
| ACMP_DRV_EnableContinuous() | Enables continuous scan mode at runtime. |
| ACMP_DRV_DisableContinuous() | Disables continuous scan mode at runtime. |

@subsection acmp_api_status Status & Output Query
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| ACMP_DRV_GetOutputFlags() | Reads output event flags for edge or level detection. |
| ACMP_DRV_ClearOutputFlags() | Clears output event flags. |
| ACMP_DRV_GetChannelFlags() | Reads per-channel change flags for continuous mode. |
| ACMP_DRV_ClearChannelFlags() | Clears per-channel change flags. |
| ACMP_DRV_GetChannelId() | Reports the channel currently being sampled in continuous mode. |
| ACMP_DRV_GetOutput() | Reads the current comparator output level. |
| ACMP_DRV_GetChannelOutput() | Reads the most recent output captured for a specific continuous-scan channel. |

@section acmp_notes Important Notes

@warning `ACMP_DRV_GetDefaultConfig()` and `ACMP_DRV_GetConfigAll()` dereference
the member pointers inside `acmp_config_t`. All four sub-structure pointers
must point to valid writable storage before calling either function.

@warning Window and filter functionality are not available in STOP modes.
Attempting to rely on those paths during STOP-mode operation can lead to
missing events or stale comparison results.

@note `ACMP_DRV_GetChannelFlags()` is primarily useful for continuous or
round-robin wakeup handling. Read the flags promptly and clear them with
`ACMP_DRV_ClearChannelFlags()` after servicing the event.

@note `ACMP_DRV_ConfigContinuous()` configures the scan engine, but some devices
also expose explicit runtime enable control. Use `ACMP_DRV_EnableContinuous()`
and `ACMP_DRV_DisableContinuous()` when the application needs to start or stop
continuous mode after initialization.

@note Optional fields such as DAC reference source, DAC output enable, clock
source selection, or one-shot trigger gating are device dependent and guarded
by `FEATURE_ACMP_*` macros.

@note On derivatives that use ACMP as a standby wakeup source, additional wakeup
controller routing may also be required outside the ACMP driver.

@section acmp_integration Integration Guide

@subsection acmp_integration_files Compilation Units
Compile the following source files into the application:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/acmp/acmp_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/acmp/acmp_hw_access.c
@endverbatim

@subsection acmp_integration_include Include Path
Add the following include paths to the toolchain configuration:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/acmp/
@endverbatim

@subsection acmp_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No additional compile symbols are required by the ACMP driver itself.

@subsection acmp_integration_deps Dependencies
- `clock_manager`
- `interrupt_manager`
- `pins`
*/
